  "scoring_semantics": {
    "ruling_verbatim": [
      "we want to score gemma's benchmark on prefill gains ^ .25 * decode ^ .75. The numbers used will be the aggregate across all 8 (summed)",
      "so when we get a baseline from the 8 baseline prompts, we add their numbers together",
      "same with the 8 golden prompts"
    ],
    "formula": "composite = prefill_gain ^ 0.25 * decode_gain ^ 0.75. Per component: gain = baseline_aggregate / candidate_aggregate (serial-anchored -- a faster candidate scores > 1, matching the family's standing convention). aggregate = the PER-STREAM SUM, i.e. each of the 8 concurrent streams' own elapsed time added together -- for prefill and decode separately, on both the baseline (serial control) leg and the candidate leg, over the SAME cohort."
  },
